{{!-- `badge-progress--modern` is opt-in via `@modern={{true}}`, passed only by classic-view's
     communicator cards. It swaps the legacy Bootstrap bar and the generic medal for the same
     treatment the Badge In Progress modal uses. The component's inline styles are suppressed
     when the flag is set (badge-progress.js) — without that the stylesheet could not reach
     these elements, since an inline style outranks it. The caseload page and the app-chrome
     inline variant pass nothing and are unaffected. --}}
<div class="badge-progress {{if this.modern 'badge-progress--modern'}}" style={{this.badge_container_style}}>
  <a href="#" {{on "click" (this.ctrlAction "badge_popup")}}>
    {{#if this.modern}}
      {{!-- LOCAL ARTWORK ONLY — the remote badge image is deliberately not requested here
           (requested 2026-09-14).

           WHY: `badge.image_url` is usually a remote OpenSymbols asset. On a cold load it is
           not in the local cache, so the browser spends a full failed round-trip to S3 before
           `onerror` fires and Button.broken_image swaps a placeholder in — the <img> is blank
           for that whole time. The placeholder was only ever a FALLBACK, so it could not be
           requested until the real URL had finished failing. Pointing `src` straight at the
           local SVG removes the network step entirely and it paints on first render.

           THE TRADE: a badge that DOES have working artwork no longer shows it on the card —
           every in-progress badge renders as the generic placeholder. The badge's name and
           its progress bar still identify it, and the modal it opens is unaffected and still
           loads the real art.

           TO REVERT: delete this branch. The `{{else if this.badge.image_url}}` below is the
           original behaviour, untouched, and is still what the caseload page and the app
           chrome use. --}}
      <img src={{path "images/badge-in-progress.svg"}} alt="" style={{this.image_style}} onerror='button_broken_image(this)' data-fallback={{path "images/badge-fallback.png"}} >
    {{else if this.badge.image_url}}
      <img src={{this.badge.image_url}} alt="" style={{this.image_style}} onerror='button_broken_image(this)' data-fallback={{path "images/badge-fallback.png"}} >
    {{else}}
      <img src={{path "images/badge-fallback.png"}} alt="" style={{this.image_style}} onerror='button_broken_image(this)' data-fallback={{path "images/badge-fallback.png"}} >
    {{/if}}
    <div class="progress" style={{this.progress_container_style}}>
      <div class="progress-bar progress-bar-warning" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow={{this.badge_progress}} aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" style={{this.progress_style}}>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>
</div>
